('my-span');\n\n    // Change color when mouse enters\n    span.addEventListener('mouseover', () => {\n      span.style.color = 'green';\n    });\n\n    // Reset color when mouse leaves\n    span.addEventListener('mouseout', () => {\n      span.style.color = 'black';\n    });\n  </script>\n\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\n### Which one should you choose?\n* Use **Method 1 (CSS)** for 99% of use cases. It is the most performant and the easiest to maintain.\n* Use **Method 2 (Inline)** if you are writing quick emails, working in a restricted CMS (like Shopify or WordPress text editors), or testing something rapidly.\n* Use **Method 3 (JavaScript)** if you want other complex actions to trigger at the exact same time the color changes.",
